# HTTP & realtime

## REST

- Base path: `/api/v1/`. URI versioning only; no breaking changes without a new version.
- JSON request/response; timestamps UTC ISO-8601; IDs as UUIDv7 for messages where spec requires.

## Errors

- Standard HTTP status codes + human-readable `message` string (SDD §13). No ad-hoc error shape per endpoint.

## Auth

- JWT access (short) + refresh in httpOnly cookie, rotation on use.
- Guest routes explicitly scoped; never reuse member middleware without guest checks.

## WebSocket

- Chat realtime on dedicated WS path; authenticate on connect.
- Support client `sync:missed` / `last_synced_message_id` per SDD §6.4 — do not invent a parallel sync protocol.

## i18n

- Backend returns **message keys** for user-facing errors where applicable; not raw English prose in domain layer.
